title: Veeam: Backup (special agent, per machine)
agents: special
catalog: os/storage
license: GPLv2
distribution: check_mk
description:
 This check monitors, on the protected machine's own host, the result of its
 last backup as reported by the Veeam Backup & Replication REST API, collected
 via the Veeam special agent. It reports the same information as the
 {VEEAM Client} service from the Veeam agent plug-in.

 This check is {OK} if the result of the last run is Success. It is {WARN}
 if the result is Warning. It is {CRIT} if the result is Failed.

 In addition {WARN} and {CRIT} levels can be set for the time since the end
 of the last backup, through the same {Veeam: Time since last backup} rule
 the {VEEAM Client} service uses. The default levels are 30 hours and 2 days.
 A finished backup without an end time is {CRIT}.

 While a backup is running, its age and duration are not evaluated. Size,
 speed and duration metrics use the same metric names as the {VEEAM Client}
 service, so existing graphs and thresholds carry over.

discovery:
 One service is created for each backup job that has processed this machine.

item:
 The name of the backup job, sanitized: spaces and apostrophes are replaced
 by underscores.
